  "description": "AWS Secrets Manager-backed IPostQuantumKeyStore for PostQuantum.DataProtection. Stores ML-KEM-768 keypairs as Secrets Manager secrets (one secret per keypair plus a small \"active\" pointer secret). The PQ secret key is already envelope-encrypted by the host IContentKeyProvider before it touches AWS, so AWS sees only opaque bytes — the service is a durable persistence target, not a new trust boundary. One-line wiring: services.AddPostQuantumDataProtectionAws(...). Multi-targets net8.0 / net9.0 / net10.0 with deterministic builds, SourceLink, and symbol packages.",
